  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "A Gu Master is someone who has opened an aperture and uses this essence to feed, refine, and manipulate Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        7
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master",
        "sys_aperture"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Inside the aperture the fluid forms a primeval sea; every drop of that seawater is pure primeval essence, the condensation of the owner’s essence, vitality, and soul.",
      "chapters": [
        6
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_primeval_sea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Essence is precious because it is the source of power for refining and using Gu. When Fang Yuan refines Moonlight Gu, a jet of essence leaves the sea and rushes into the worm; while the Gu resists, that essence can be driven back out and the gain erased unless he keeps refining and replenishes the sea.",
      "chapters": [
        10
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "spending-and-recovery",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "gu_moonlight_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Two ordinary ways restore spent essence. Natural recovery refills the sea over time: for a C grade talent about four percent of the aperture’s store per hour, or about twenty-four percent in six hours; for an A grade talent about eight percent per hour, forty-eight percent in six hours.",
      "chapters": [
        10
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "spending-and-recovery",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_c_grade",
        "sys_a_grade"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Primeval stones are the external supplement. A Gu Master can extract essence from a stone to raise the sea’s water level, so stones are both currency and cultivation fuel.",
      "chapters": [
        8
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "spending-and-recovery",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_primeval_stones"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Talent still caps how high the sea can stand: Fang Yuan cannot store past forty-four percent even when empty space remains above the surface.",
      "chapters": [
        10
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "spending-and-recovery",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_aptitude"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Essence becomes more concise as the Gu Master advances. Essence at rank one is green copper, at rank two red iron, and at rank three white silver.",
      "chapters": [
        22
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "color-and-density-by-rank",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "One portion of red iron equals ten of green copper, and one portion of white silver equals ten of red iron.",
      "chapters": [
        26
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "color-and-density-by-rank",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Essence at rank four is yellow gold.",
      "chapters": [
        55
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "color-and-density-by-rank",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dedicated pages cover green copper, red steel, and white silver. Red iron and red steel both name this rank two tier.",
      "chapters": [
        152
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "color-and-density-by-rank",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_green_copper_primeval_essence",
        "sys_red_steel_primeval_essence",
        "sys_white_silver_primeval_essence"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rank ladder around those tiers is on ranks and realms.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "color-and-density-by-rank",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_ranks_and_realms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu Masters at rank five have purple crystal primeval essence. Initial stage is light purple, middle stage violet purple, upper stage deep purple, and peak stage crystal purple.",
      "chapters": [
        379
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rank-five-essence",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    }
  ],
